<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><ns3:refentry xmlns:ns3="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0" xml:id="man.indent.lists" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"><ns3:refmeta><ns3:refentrytitle>man.indent.lists</ns3:refentrytitle><ns3:refmiscinfo class="other" otherclass="datatype">boolean</ns3:refmiscinfo></ns3:refmeta><ns3:refnamediv><ns3:refname>man.indent.lists</ns3:refname><ns3:refpurpose>Adjust indentation of lists?</ns3:refpurpose></ns3:refnamediv><ns3:refsynopsisdiv><ns4:fragment xmlns:ns4="http://nwalsh.com/xmlns/litprog/fragment" xml:id="man.indent.lists.frag"><ns5:param xmlns:ns5="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Transform" name="man.indent.lists" select="1"/></ns4:fragment></ns3:refsynopsisdiv><ns3:refsection><ns3:info><ns3:title>Description</ns3:title></ns3:info><ns3:para>If the value of <ns3:parameter>man.indent.lists</ns3:parameter> is
non-zero, the width of the left margin for list items in
<ns3:tag>itemizedlist</ns3:tag>,
<ns3:tag>orderedlist</ns3:tag>,
<ns3:tag>variablelist</ns3:tag> output (and output of some other
lists) is set to the value of the
<ns3:parameter>man.indent.width</ns3:parameter> parameter
(<ns3:literal>4n</ns3:literal> by default). If instead the value of
<ns3:parameter>man.indent.lists</ns3:parameter> is zero, the built-in roff
default width (<ns3:literal>7.2n</ns3:literal>) is used.</ns3:para></ns3:refsection></ns3:refentry>